-- the oriented orbits refine the graph's: atoms the orientation keeps apart may be identified by the
-- bond graph, and never the other way. So a signal count read off the graph is an upper bound on the
-- equivalences that hold, and the spectrum that disagrees with it is not the spectrum's error.
or-orbit-refines : (S : Oriented) → (x : mol-atoms (or-mol S)) → (y : mol-atoms (or-mol S)) → OrOrbit S x y → Orbit (or-mol S) x y
or-orbit-refines S x y o = (fst (fst o) , snd o)
